[Event "Queen's Gambit vs QGD"]

{2.c4 attacks d5 from the side. Against the Declined White aims for Bg5, e3 and either a minority attack or central play.}
1. d4 {[%csl Ge5,Gc5] Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
1... d5 {Symmetry. The pawn on d5 controls e4.}
2. c4 {[%cal Gc4d5] The Queen's Gambit: c4 trades a wing pawn for a centre pawn.}
2... e6 {The QGD: rock solid, but the c8-bishop is locked in.}
3. Nc3 {Adds pressure on d5. The knight on c3 eyes the pawn on d5 and controls e4.}
3... Nf6 {Defends d5. The knight on f6 controls e4.}
4. Bg5 {[%cal Gg5f6] Pins the defender of d5. The bishop on g5 eyes the knight on f6.}
4... Be7 {Breaks the pin.}
 (4... Nbd7 {Hides the Elephant Trap. The knight on d7 controls e5.}
5. cxd5 {Exchange. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e6.}
5... exd5 {Recaptures. The pawn on d5 controls e4.}
6. e3 {Do not take d5: 6.Nxd5?? Nxd5 7.Bxd8 Bb4+ loses a piece.}
6... c6 {Solid.}
7. Bd3 {Develops. The bishop on d3 eyes the pawn on h7 and controls e4.}
)
5. e3 {Solid development.}
5... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
6... h6 {Asks the bishop. The pawn on h6 eyes the bishop on g5.}
7. Bh4 {Keeps the pin. The bishop on h4 eyes the knight on f6.}
7... b6 {The Tartakower: the bishop goes to b7.}
8. Be2 {Develops.}
8... Bb7 {Develops on the long diagonal.}
9. Bxf6 {Trades to weaken d5. The bishop on f6 eyes the bishop on e7 and the pawn on g7 and controls e5.}
9... Bxf6 {Recaptures. The bishop on f6 eyes the pawn on d4 and controls e5.}
10. cxd5 {Opens the c-file. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e6.}
10... exd5 {Recaptures. The pawn on d5 controls e4.}
11. b4 {[%cal Gb4b5] A minority attack.} *

[Event "Queen's Gambit Exchange"]

{The Exchange gives the Carlsbad structure: a minority attack on the queenside.}
1. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
1... d5 {Symmetry. The pawn on d5 controls e4.}
2. c4 {Queen's Gambit. The pawn on c4 eyes the pawn on d5.}
2... e6 {QGD.}
3. Nc3 {Pressure. The knight on c3 eyes the pawn on d5 and controls e4.}
3... Nf6 {Defends. The knight on f6 controls e4.}
4. cxd5 {The Exchange. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e6.}
4... exd5 {Recaptures. The pawn on d5 controls e4.}
5. Bg5 {Pins. The bishop on g5 eyes the knight on f6.}
5... c6 {Solid.}
6. Qc2 {[%cal Gc2h7] Stops ...Bf5 ideas and eyes h7. The queen on c2 eyes the pawn on h7 and controls e4.}
6... Be7 {Develops.}
7. e3 {Solid.}
7... Nbd7 {Develops. The knight on d7 controls e5.}
8. Bd3 {[%cal Gd3h7] Develops toward the kingside. The bishop on d3 eyes the pawn on h7 and controls e4.}
8... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9. Nge2 {A flexible setup that allows f3 and e4.} *

[Event "Queen's Gambit Accepted"]

{After 2...dxc4 White simply recovers the pawn with e3 and Bxc4.}
1. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
1... d5 {Symmetry. The pawn on d5 controls e4.}
2. c4 {Queen's Gambit. The pawn on c4 eyes the pawn on d5.}
2... dxc4 {Accepts, giving up the centre.}
3. Nf3 {Stops ...e5. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
3... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
4. e3 {Opens the bishop to take c4.}
4... e6 {Solid. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
5. Bxc4 {Regains the pawn. The bishop on c4 eyes the pawn on e6 and controls d5.}
5... c5 {Hits d4. The pawn on c5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... a6 {Prepares ...b5.}
7. a4 {[%cal Ga4b5] Stops ...b5.} *

[Event "Queen's Gambit vs Slav, Albin & Chigorin"]

{Other replies to 2.c4: the Slav, the Albin Countergambit and the Chigorin.}
1. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
1... d5 {Symmetry. The pawn on d5 controls e4.}
2. c4 {Queen's Gambit. The pawn on c4 eyes the pawn on d5.}
2... c6 {The Slav.}
 (2... e5 {The Albin Countergambit. The pawn on e5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
3. dxe5 {Takes.}
3... d4 {Gains space.}
4. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on d4.}
4... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on e5.}
5. g3 {The bishop goes to g2.}
)
 (2... Nc6 {The Chigorin. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on d4 and controls e5.}
3. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
3... Bg4 {Pins. The bishop on g4 eyes the knight on f3.}
4. cxd5 {Takes. The pawn on d5 eyes the knight on c6.}
4... Bxf3 {Trades. The bishop on f3 eyes the pawn on d5 and the pawn on e2 and controls e4.}
5. gxf3 {Recaptures. The pawn on f3 controls e4.}
5... Qxd5 {Recaptures. The queen on d5 eyes the pawn on d4 and the pawn on f3 and controls e4 and e5.}
6. e3 {Solid; White has the bishop pair.}
)
3. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
3... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls e4.}
4. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 eyes the pawn on d5 and controls e4.}
4... dxc4 {Takes.}
5. a4 {[%cal Ga4b5] Stops ...b5.}
5... Bf5 {Develops outside the chain. The bishop on f5 controls e4.}
6. e3 {Prepares Bxc4.}
6... e6 {Solid. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
7. Bxc4 {Regains the pawn. The bishop on c4 eyes the pawn on e6 and controls d5.}
7... Bb4 {Pins the knight. The bishop on b4 eyes the knight on c3.}
8. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.} *
